==================================================================================
PARITY (web VehicleCharts.tsx -> native), no scope narrowing
==================================================================================
  - Live-map guard `state.latitude && state.longitude` (JS truthiness, 0 falsy) ->
    VehicleChartsStateRecord.currentCoordinate (drops 0 / NaN / nil) — tested.
  - Trail `positions.filter(p => p.latitude && p.longitude).map([lat,lng])` ->
    VehicleChartsProjection.trail (same truthiness filter, source order) — tested.
  - Speed series `positions.map(p => ({ time: formatTime(p.ts), speed:
    p.speed_mph != null ? convertSpeedFromSI(p.speed_mph) : null })).reverse()` ->
    VehicleChartsProjection.speedSeries: oldest-first (reverse), a real 0 kept, nil/NaN
    dropped; SI -> display unit converted at the RENDER boundary via the useUnits seam
    (ADR-009: speed_mph is the legacy name for an SI m/s value) — tested.
    Platform adaptation (NOT scope narrowing): a sample with no finite speed is omitted
    rather than drawn as a Recharts connectNulls gap; every real-speed point is plotted,
    and the friendly "Position data will appear here" shows when there is no speed.
  - Vehicle Configuration `MetricCard` array (18 tiles) -> VehicleChartsConfigTiles.make:
    cleanNil passthrough (Model..Charge Port..), boolean tokens (Europe/RHD -> Yes/No,
    Remote Start -> Active/Off, Offroad Lightbar -> Present/No), `${pct}%` (SW Download/
    Install), and the `|| 'Not Installed'` / `|| 'None'` / `|| '—'` fallbacks — every
    branch ported + tested (count/order == the web array, sentinel -> em-dash).
  - Car Display Preferences `MetricCard` array (5 tiles) -> VehicleChartsPreferenceTiles.make
    via the parseSettingEnum port (Distance/Temperature/Charge Unit/Tire Pressure/24h Time)
    — tested (DistanceUnitMiles -> Miles, PressureUnitPsi -> PSI, missing -> em-dash).
  - Recharts speed `<AreaChart>` (areaGradient cyan + ChartTooltip) -> Swift Charts AreaMark
    (translucent chartSeriesSpeed gradient) under a 2pt LineMark, monotone interpolation,
    chartXSelection tooltip + RuleMark/PointMark, and an AXChartDescriptor exposing every
    (time, speed) point ("view as table"). Axes on the token dashed grid.
  - Leaflet MapContainer+MapTileLayer+Marker(vehicleIcon)+Polyline(#00f0ff)+MapLayerSwitcher
    -> MapKit Map + car-glyph accent pin + cyan MapPolyline (only when trail.count > 1) +
    segmented map-style switcher; camera frames current+trail via the shared, unit-tested
    TSGeo.boundingRegion, falling back to the current position at a zoom-14-equivalent span.
    Footer `${fmtNumber(lat)}, ${fmtNumber(lng)}` -> mono coordinate readout + a11y label.
  - All 9 web i18n keys reproduced verbatim (common.location/.vehicleConfig/.carPreferences/
    .speedHistory/.positionDataWillAppear/.yes/.no, vehicles.detail.europeVehicle/.rhd);
    every label the web HARDCODED in English (Model, Trim, Active, Not Installed, Miles, ...)
    is localized through the per-surface table. 63 catalog keys; 0 English literal in code
    (verified: every localize()/string() key resolves to a catalog entry).
  - States: loading (skeleton), loaded (composite), empty (friendly — no map/config/prefs/
    speed), error (QueryError+retry), stale (chip+refresh), offline (cached+chip) — all
    rendered, never blank. The Speed History panel is ALWAYS present in the composite (web
    parity) with its own no-data message.
  - A11y: section headers = .isHeader; each metric tile = one combined "label, value" element;
    map labelled + marker labelled; speed chart = AXChartDescriptor + container label; coord
    footer labelled; decorative glyphs accessibilityHidden; Reduce-Motion honored (skeleton +
    transitions via TSAnimation/TSSkeleton); Dynamic Type via the system-font token ramp.
  - Telemetry: VehicleChartsSurface.slug="VehicleCharts" emitted via P1/S11 view.opened on
    appear (idempotent), os_log default sink, redaction-safe (no VIN/coord/speed/config).

